       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day. That is twice the labeled maximum for adults, which is 3,200 mg/day under prescription supervision. The usual OTC limit is 1,200 mg/day. A dose that high carries a serious risk of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events. Normal kidney and liver function doesn't change that limit.\n\nThese are options within the labeled limit:\n- **800 mg PO four times daily** (3,200 mg/day), which is the maximum.\n- **600 mg PO four times daily** (2,400 mg/day).\n- **400 mg PO every 4\u20136 hours as needed**, for pain or fever.\n\nIf you meant a different dose, such as 800 mg or 1600 mg total per day, tell me the dose and frequency and I'll enter it. Consider GI protection if the patient needs sustained high-dose therapy."
